# Public release allowlist: every new/unreviewed file is ignored by default.
# Add a path only after reviewing its contents for public disclosure.
# This excludes operational launchers, local configuration, credentials, wallets,
# logs, inventories, migration records, backups, private RTL and all other images.
# Only the exact reviewed source, documentation and PoC assets below are allowed.
#
# IMPORTANT: .gitignore cannot protect edits inside already-tracked files and
# can be bypassed by git add -f. Content review and publication safeguards remain
# necessary. Never publish a private development/production checkout directly.

*

